  "two_halves_of_the_geometry": {
    "baseline_serving_slot_tokens": 24576,
    "baseline_serving_slots": 1,
    "fragment_c": 24576,
    "fragment_np": 1,
    "merge_server_args_is_identity": true,
    "why_both": "rails.adapters.runtime_view reads serving_slots/serving_slot_tokens from the composed values as the adapter's flight-side geometry; core.flight.FlightRuntime.serve writes that geometry back over the fragment's -np/-c through merge_server_args and builds the required session identity from the result, and the dispatcher sizes its concurrency by slots (workers = slots, so this flight submits ONE request at a time). A baseline that still said serving_slots 4 would demand -np 4 -c 98304 of the resident session and be refused. The geometry therefore moves serving_slots in the baseline as well as the fragment's flags, and the composed diff below names it as the one non-bookkeeping baseline key that moves. No code change is needed to express -np 1 or the prompt cache off; the legacy speech-native PROFILE driver's KV-policy binder (core.driver.speech_native.profile_agent_kv_policy) does require --cache-prompt, but it is reached only from the saea-driver speech-native-profile CLI, never from FlightRuntime."
  },
  "why_no_cache_prompt_is_explicit": "llama.cpp (the pinned featcache checkout, common/common.h) defaults cache_prompt to TRUE and exposes --cache-prompt / --no-cache-prompt as a boolean pair (common/arg.cpp); the server's per-request cache_prompt field defaults to the server value (tools/server/server-schema.cpp) and this study's transport sends none, so the prompt cache is OFF only when the server is started with --no-cache-prompt. With it the server sets n_past = 0 for every request (tools/server/server-context.cpp: 'if we don't cache the prompt, we have to remove all previous tokens') and re-processes the whole prompt from an empty KV cache. --slot-prompt-similarity governs which idle slot a request is routed to by cached-prefix similarity; with one slot and no cache it has no object."
}
